## 1. Problem framing and opportunity solution tree

### 1.1 Problem statement

For Medicare-heavy, multi-location DME suppliers, the final moment of leverage is **before equipment is released**. Yet evidence arrives fragmented across fax, PDFs, EHR messages, portals, e-prescribing networks, calls, and the supplier’s ERP. Intake staff must translate changing public rules—regulations, NCDs, LCDs, policy articles, Standard Documentation Requirements, PA lists, and DME MAC guidance—into order-level checks. A document can exist but be unusable: wrong beneficiary, stale encounter, missing signature/date, wrong item detail, conflicting quantity, or an order created after delivery when WOPD applied.

The current process is memory-driven and lossy. Staff repeatedly open documents, use local checklists, chase clinics, re-key status, and release under shipment pressure. The defect then becomes expensive: delayed cash, denial rework, an ADR response, TPE scrutiny, RAC recoupment, or an unrecoverable shipment. CMS’s Targeted Probe and Educate (TPE) generally reviews 20–40 claims per round; problems not improved after three rounds may lead to 100% prepayment review, extrapolation, Recovery Auditor referral, or other action ([CMS TPE](https://www.cms.gov/data-research/monitoring-programs/medicare-fee-service-compliance-programs/medical-review-and-education/targeted-probe-and-educate-tpe)).

### 1.2 Target segment and desired outcome

**Beachhead ICP:** US DME suppliers with ≥1,000 Medicare orders/month, centralized intake, multiple active locations, material volume in CGM/supplies, PAP/resupply, oxygen, selected orthoses, or pneumatic compression, and operations spanning two DME MAC footprints.

**Desired outcome:** Increase the percentage of Medicare orders that are **human-released with complete, source-linked, rule-version-correct administrative evidence before fulfillment**, while reducing cycle time and touches.

**Outcome boundary:** “Documentation ready” means evidence satisfies an approved administrative checklist. It is **not** a medical-necessity, coverage, coding, or device recommendation.

### 1.3 Opportunity solution tree

| Desired outcome | Opportunity / unmet need | Candidate solution | Riskiest experiment |
|---|---|---|---|
| Human-released, evidence-complete order before ship | Staff cannot reliably know which version of which rule applied on DOS | Human-approved Criteria Skills; deterministic HCPCS/DOS/jurisdiction selector; effective-date regression suite | Blind replay across 1,000 orders and policy-change boundary cases; zero silent version errors |
| Same | Evidence is buried in mixed faxes and PDFs | Fax splitting, OCR, classification, entity reconciliation, signature/date detection, page-level evidence graph | Compare against dual-abstracted gold set; ≥90% critical-gap recall and ≥95% release-ready precision |
| Same | “Document received” is confused with “criterion satisfied” | Five-state criterion status: Present, Missing, Conflicting, Uncertain, N/A; source citation beside every status | Moderated review with 12 intake users; ≥10/12 reach correct action without assistance |
| Same | Chasing a clinic is slow, interruptive, and unauditable | Owner-specific cure plan; no-login guest link; reminders; secure upload/acknowledgment; handshake history | 100 real guest tasks; ≥60% completed within two business days, no PHI leakage |
| Same | Shipment pressure overrides incomplete evidence | Ranked hold queue by ship date and allowed dollars; human release; reason-coded override; supervisor escalation | Shadow mode then controlled release; no autonomous release and ≥95% override attribution |
| Same | Audit response reconstructs history months later | Sealed packet: manifest, evidence index, criteria version/citations, actions, reviewer, timestamps, hashes | Compliance blind test: build 30 packets manually vs DocLock; ≥50% faster, 100% source traceability |
| Same | Existing systems already own order/billing workflow | Overlay via fax/PDF first, then Brightree/NikoHealth/WellSky/Parachute and EHR interfaces | Technical spike in two partner environments; ≥95% order matching, no ERP write corruption |

### 1.4 Why this solution—not a generic AI copilot

Probabilistic models are suitable for **assistive evidence processing** but not the controlling conclusion. Only approved deterministic Criteria Skills may set gap status. Every machine extraction retains page coordinates, confidence, source hash, and model/version metadata; low confidence becomes **Uncertain**, never silently Present. A human sees the evidence and makes the release decision. This separation is the core product thesis and the primary regulatory/ethical control.

