### 2.4 Ecosystem and competitive context

DocLock must overlay, not disparage, systems already delivering value. Brightree positions its HME/DME platform around billing, patient engagement, analytics, ePrescribe, referral, and intake workflows ([Brightree](https://www.brightree.com/hme-dme-software/)). NikoHealth markets fax-to-classified-record and prefilled-order intake automation ([NikoHealth](https://nikohealth.com/)). WellSky’s Bonafide platform spans order processing, compliance, inventory, and billing ([WellSky](https://wellsky.com/dme-hme-software/)). Parachute supports structured digital ordering, status, documentation capture, AI intake, and clinician requests ([Parachute](https://explore.parachutehealth.com/digital-order-management-platform-and-ai-intake)). DocLock’s defendable layer is effective-dated criteria governance, evidence-level deterministic status, human release control, cross-channel cure, and sealed memory—not generic intake or e-prescribing.

