### 3.3 Regulatory moments that shape the journey

The Standard Documentation Requirements article A55426 states that an SWO must be communicated before claim submission and that, for items on the required list, a WOPD must be received before delivery; supplier documentation must be maintained for seven years from DOS ([CMS A55426](https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=55426)). DocLock therefore stores the received timestamp, source, signature/date evidence, delivery timestamp, and policy version separately. It must never “repair” timing through backdating.

Jurisdiction is not simply the supplier branch: the beneficiary’s permanent address determines DME MAC jurisdiction. The initial two-footprint implementation must cover Noridian JA/JD and CGS JB/JC while testing state mapping and beneficiary-address change cases. Policy hierarchy and conflicts must route to compliance as **Uncertain**, never resolve by model preference.

