## 5. Solution ideation and concept definition

### 5.1 Selected concept

**DME DocLock v1 is an operator-facing gate and collaboration overlay.** It receives an order packet; creates a source-preserving evidence graph; selects an approved Criteria Skill deterministically; evaluates evidence into five explicit states; builds a cure plan; supports a secure guest exchange; continuously reevaluates; and presents an authorized human with release, hold, or reason-coded override. It seals the state and provenance packet at each consequential decision.

**Concept flow**

1. **Ingest:** fax/PDF plus CSV/API order metadata; malware scan, immutable original, SHA-256 hash, source timestamp.
2. **Understand assistively:** classify/split, OCR, extract entities, detect signatures/dates, reconcile patient/prescriber/order. Model output is proposed evidence, not policy.
3. **Select rules deterministically:** HCPCS/product family + DOS + beneficiary jurisdiction + PA/workflow flags resolve to an approved effective-dated Criteria Skill.
4. **Evaluate:** each criterion is Present, Missing, Conflicting, Uncertain, or N/A with page-level source and explanation.
5. **Cure:** assign an authorized owner, create a concise request, use a no-account expiring guest link, record every action, and ingest returned originals.
6. **Decide:** ranked work queue; human opens critical evidence and chooses release, hold, or override under role and reason controls.
7. **Remember:** seal manifest, criteria/version/citations, source index, extraction lineage, guest history, reviewer identity, timestamps, reason, and hashes.

### 5.2 v1 scope

| In v1 | Boundary / acceptance |
|---|---|
| Segments | ≥1,000 Medicare orders/month; centralized intake; multi-location; two partner-confirmed footprints among Noridian JA/JD and CGS JB/JC |
| Product families | CGM and supplies; PAP and resupply; oxygen; selected orthoses and pneumatic compression only after criteria validation |
| Channels | Fax and PDF day one; secure upload; batch/API metadata. Epic and Oracle Health FHIR R4/DocumentReference read spike behind feature flag—Oracle documents R4 4.0.1 and DocumentReference read support ([Oracle Health](https://docs.oracle.com/en/industries/health/millennium-platform-apis/mfrap/api-documentreference.html)); Epic publishes R4 resources ([Epic on FHIR](https://fhir.epic.com/)) |
| Rules | Public CMS, NCD/LCD, related policy articles, A55426, PA lists, and Noridian/CGS guidance; human-authored and two-person approved; effective dated |
| Checks | SWO/WOPD timing and elements, signature/date presence, encounter/document freshness, PA applicability/status evidence, continued-use/continued-need administrative evidence, modifier-supporting administrative facts, internal conflicts |
| Workflow | Queue, evidence viewer, cure plan, guest task, reminders, continuous reevaluation, human release/hold/override, supervisor escalation |
| Governance | SSO/RBAC, BAA, encryption, tenant isolation, least privilege, immutable audit trail, retention/export/delete policy, policy publish/rollback |
| Packet | Original manifest, evidence index, criteria version and public citations, statuses, handshake, reviewer/decision, hashes; clearly labeled operational record, not “audit-proof” certification |

### 5.3 Explicitly out of scope

- Medical-necessity or coverage determinations; clinical appropriateness; diagnosis inference; device/product recommendations.
- Autonomous release, fulfillment, claim submission, PA submission, appeals, attestation, signature, or alteration of a note/order.
- Generated clinical language, suggested charting intended to satisfy coverage, backdating, cloned signatures, or filling absent facts.
- Coding optimization, fee-schedule optimization, ABN determination, beneficiary inducement, or contingency-fee recovery.
- Redistribution of MCG, InterQual, payer-proprietary policies, or copyrighted material without license.
- Replacing Brightree, NikoHealth, WellSky, Parachute, EHR, clearinghouse, inventory, billing, CRM, or fax.
- Medicaid, Medicare Advantage payer-specific policy, commercial payers, all HCPCS, all four footprints at launch, or international use.
- Two-sided payer adoption dependency; prescriber analytics/ranking; model training on tenant PHI without explicit contractual basis.

### 5.4 Regulatory, privacy, and clinical constraints

DocLock is a HIPAA business associate when it handles PHI for suppliers; deployment requires a BAA, minimum-necessary access, security risk analysis, incident response, subcontractor controls, and customer-configured retention consistent with law and contract. A55426’s seven-year supplier documentation obligation informs default preservation but does not authorize indefinite storage. Legal counsel must assess state retention, electronic-signature, recording, and patient-access requirements.

The product UI must say **“administrative evidence status”**, not “covered,” “medically necessary,” or “approved.” A status never edits source evidence. Policy citations link to the exact public version and effective period. Any policy ambiguity, model uncertainty, mismatched patient, or unavailable source blocks “ready” and routes to an authorized human.

