## 7. Success metrics

### 7.1 North Star

**Evidence-Complete Human Release Rate (ECHRR):**

> Number of in-scope Medicare orders released by an authorized human with all applicable administrative criteria Present or validly N/A, exact approved Criteria Skill/version, and complete source provenance **before fulfillment**, divided by all in-scope Medicare orders released.

Report ECHRR by product family, location, jurisdiction, order channel, and override status. Do not improve it by holding everything: cycle-time and patient-access guardrails counterbalance it.

### 7.2 Metric tree

| Type | Metric | Definition / 90-day target |
|---|---|---|
| North Star | ECHRR | Baseline then +20 percentage points or ≥90%, while quality guardrails hold |
| Input | Eligible-order coverage | ≥90% of scoped orders successfully ingested and matched |
| Input | Criteria coverage | 100% of enabled HCPCS/DOS/jurisdiction combinations have approved, tested version; otherwise block |
| Input | Evidence extraction traceability | 100% of displayed facts link to source page/region and source hash |
| Input | Guest task clarity | ≥60% completed within two business days; median active time ≤4 min |
| Input | Operator adoption | ≥85% weekly active among assigned users; ≥90% release decisions made in workflow during controlled phase |
| Process | Documentation chase rate | Track, not necessarily minimize; distinguish correctly detected chase from avoidable chase |
| Process | Touches per chased order | ≥30% reduction vs matched baseline |
| Process | Median referral-to-ready | ≥20% reduction; report p90 to expose long tail |
| Process | Human review time | Median <3 min; p95 <8 min |
| Output | Release-ready precision | ≥95%; never trade down for volume |
| Output | Critical-gap recall | ≥90% overall and no critical class below 85% without disabling that class |
| Output | Documentation-denial rate | ≥30% relative reduction or touches target met within 90 days; adjudicated subset only |
| Output | Audit packet preparation | ≥50% reduction with zero source omissions attributable to export |
| Output | Allowed dollars exposed | Sum allowed amount on released orders later found to have curable pre-ship defects; downward trend |
| Business | Paid ACV / retention | 3 partners ≥$24K ACV; expansion intent and renewal evidence by day 90 |

### 7.3 Guardrails and stop metrics

| Guardrail | Threshold / response |
|---|---|
| Autonomous consequential action | **0** autonomous releases, claims, attestations, note edits, or device recommendations; any event = pause |
| Silent policy-version error | **0**; any event disables affected criteria and triggers incident review |
| Wrong-patient/unauthorized PHI disclosure | **0**; incident response, link revocation, pilot pause |
| Source alteration or fabricated language | **0**; originals immutable; any event = critical incident |
| False-ready rate | ≤5% on adjudicated sample; weekly compliance sampling, category disable if exceeded |
| False-hold / patient access | <5% of holds adjudicated unnecessary; no increase >10% in urgent-order delay; escalation SLA <2 h |
| Override rate | <10% overall; 100% reason-coded/attributable; >15% by user/category triggers review—not punitive surveillance |
| Workflow burden | No >10% increase in median total handling time after week 4 |
| Bias / access | Compare guest completion and delay by clinic size, rurality where available, language/channel, disability-access needs; >10-point unexplained gap requires remediation |
| Availability / integrity | ≥99.9% production availability after pilot; RPO ≤15 min, RTO ≤4 h; no lost originals |

Metrics must use pre-registered definitions, matched cohorts where possible, confidence intervals, and exclusion logs. A fall in denial rate is lagging and confounded by case mix, payer edits, and staff behavior; touches and ECHRR provide earlier evidence but do not substitute for financial outcomes.

